Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: reserve headroom when aligning empty RX skbs

The refill and monitor-status paths align a newly allocated, empty skb
with skb_pull(). A non-zero alignment delta exceeds skb->len, so the
pull is rejected and the data pointer stays unaligned. Use skb_reserve()
before DMA mapping. The existing allocation includes an extra alignment
unit, leaving at least DP_RX_BUFFER_SIZE bytes after the reservation.

This carries only the alignment correction from OpenWrt PR #24254,
commit 2ab272d5bdab22626bc67a08906e2ed9fabd44b7, by Mark Ruvald Pedersen.
Keep the local 984 kmalloc allocation and NSS/IRQ recovery changes;
do not introduce the PR's private page-frag allocator or teardown hooks.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24254
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -379,7 +379,7 @@ int ath11k_dp_rxbufs_replenish(struct ath11k_base *ab, int mac_id,
 		if (!IS_ALIGNED((unsigned long)skb->data,
 				DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE)) {
-			skb_pull(skb,
+			skb_reserve(skb,
 				 PTR_ALIGN(skb->data, DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE) -
 				 skb->data);
 		}
 
@@ -2846,7 +2846,7 @@ static struct sk_buff *ath11k_dp_rx_alloc_mon_status_buf(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 	if (!IS_ALIGNED((unsigned long)skb->data,
 			DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE)) {
-		skb_pull(skb, PTR_ALIGN(skb->data, DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE) -
+		skb_reserve(skb, PTR_ALIGN(skb->data, DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE) -
 			 skb->data);
 	}
 
 	paddr = dma_map_single(ab->dev, skb->data,
